of the format, not a bug; == on floats is almost always wrong","Compare with a tolerance: absolute near zero, relative elsewhere; or count the distance in ulps","Subtracting close numbers loses digits, and big plus small swallows the small; Kahan accumulates the loss"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["double s = 0.1 + 0.2;","s == 0.3        // 0","s - 0.3         // 5.55e-17"],"hl":[1],"lang":"c","size":10.5,"lh":24.0,"w":320.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":10.0,"y":36.0,"lines":["int near(double a, double b) {","    double d = fabs(a - b);","    return d <= 1e-9 || d <= 1e-9 * fmax(fabs(a), fabs(b));","}"],"hl":[2],"lang":"c","size":8.5,"lh":22.0,"w":350.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":10.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["double sum = 0, c = 0;","for (…) { double y = x[i] - c;","         double t = sum + y;","         c = (t - sum) - y; sum = t; }"],"hl":[3],"lang":"c","size":9.0,"lh":22.0,"w":345.0}]],"cues":[13.4,25.6]}]},{"title":"Special values","sub":"NaN, inf, −0","short":"NaN","main":"isnan; integer divide by zero is UB; careful casting to int.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["NaN","Division and zero","To integer"],"captions":["NaN equals nothing, even itself: test with isnan(x); infinity with isinf(x)","Float divided by zero is infinity, 0.0/0.0 is NaN, but integer divide by zero is undefined; −0.0 equals +0.0","Casting to integer drops the fraction; out of range is UB; rounding: floor, ceil, round, rint"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["double x = 0.0 / 0.0;","x == x          // 0","isnan(x)        // 1"],"hl":[2],"lang":"c","size":11.0,"lh":24.0,"w":320.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":36.0,"lines":["1.0 / 0.0     //  inf","-1.0 / 0.0    // -inf","1 / 0          // ✕ UB (integers)"],"bad":[2],"lang":"c","size":10.5,"lh":24.0,"w":320.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["(int)3.99      // 3","(int)-3.99     // -3","(int)1e20      // ✕ UB","round(2.5)      // 3.0"],"bad":[2],"lang":"c","size":10.5,"lh":22.0,"w":320.0}]],"cues":[9.5,24.9]}]},{"title":"Data encoding","sub":"varint, base64, UTF-8, CRC","short":"Encoding","main":"Network order, variable length and checksums.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Network and varint","Hex and base64","UTF-8 and CRC"],"captions":["Integers go in network order byte by byte; varint packs 7 bits per byte, so small values take one byte","Binary data as text: hexadecimal digits or base64, where three bytes become four characters","UTF-8: 1 to 4 bytes per character, high bits show where it starts; CRC catches random storage and transfer errors"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":10.0,"y":36.0,"lines":["300  →  0xAC 0x02","// 300 = 0b100101100","// low 7 bits: 0101100 | 0x80 = 0xAC, then 0x02"],"lang":"c","size":9.5,"lh":24.0,"w":345.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":70.0,"y":60.0,"w":150.0,"h":28.0,"text":"\"Man\" = 4D 61 6E","tone":"blue","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":270.0,"y":60.0,"w":100.0,"h":28.0,"text":"\"TWFu\"","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e","x1":150.0,"y1":60.0,"x2":216.0,"y2":60.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":116.0,"text":"24 bits → 4 × 6 bits → 4 characters","size":9.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":10.0,"y":28.0,"lines":["0xxxxxxx                      1 byte","110xxxxx 10xxxxxx             2","1110xxxx 10xxxxxx 10xxxxxx    3","11110xxx 10xxxxxx 10xxxxxx 10xxxxxx"],"lang":"c","size":8.5,"lh":20.0,"w":345.0}]],"cues":[14.9,25.1]}]},{"title":"Summary","sub":"What's next","short":"Summary","main":"Next: linking, make and libraries.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Bytes and bits","Floating point","Next"],"captions":["Memory is bytes; a type is a way to read them; signed overflow is UB; byte order is platform-specific; read representation via memcpy","Structs have padding; bit-fields are not for protocols; compare floats with a tolerance and mind special values","Next we build a program from several files: linking, librarie